        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 2218
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-12-11T15:54:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, this was more a vestige of the refactoring, and can be reversed.  I did feel it was slightly better self documenting this way:  contrast\n\nself.identity_api\n\nwith \n\nself.api.identity\n\nIt did make it easier to migrate the responsibility for building the set of APIs around, as it was originally done in service.py.  For a while, until I figured how I was triggereing the to the circular depenedency, I was building these in the individual controllers as well.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAMX//3/M\u003d",
      "revId": "c0967193c679b2dacbc0b94245d43f7882d4e5b2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
